  "id": "illusory-contour",
  "term": "illusory contour",
  "definition": "An illusory contour is a perceived edge or shape, such as a Kanizsa figure, that the visual system experiences even though no actual contour is physically drawn. It depends on surrounding visual context that induces the impression of a boundary or form.",
